00:56:06.727 --> 00:56:08.600
EMILIO: Yeah, sure.

00:56:08.600 --> 00:56:09.680
Hi.

00:56:09.680 --> 00:56:12.770
How did the COVID
experience affected

00:56:12.770 --> 00:56:15.860
your parameter estimation
process or your overall scoring

00:56:15.860 --> 00:56:18.450
process?

00:56:18.450 --> 00:56:19.050
I'm sorry?

00:56:19.050 --> 00:56:21.750
I didn't hear your question.

00:56:21.750 --> 00:56:23.130
EMILIO: Can you hear me now?

00:56:23.130 --> 00:56:23.820
RACHAEL DEMPSEY: I can hear you.

00:56:23.820 --> 00:56:24.320
Yep.

00:56:24.320 --> 00:56:24.900
YU CAO: Yep.

00:56:24.900 --> 00:56:27.090
EMILIO: How did
COVID-19 experience

00:56:27.090 --> 00:56:31.350
affected your process
of estimating parameters

00:56:31.350 --> 00:56:33.300
and the overall scoring?

00:56:33.300 --> 00:56:34.170
Thanks?

00:56:34.170 --> 00:56:38.100
Oh, it changes
everything that occurred.

00:56:38.100 --> 00:56:41.190
And not COVID-19 itself, just
because of the stimulation

00:56:41.190 --> 00:56:41.850
money.

00:56:41.850 --> 00:56:44.740
Because of stimulus money,
all the bureau scores,

00:56:44.740 --> 00:56:45.908
they are inflated.

00:56:45.908 --> 00:56:47.700
There is an inflation
in the bureau scores.

00:56:47.700 --> 00:56:50.670
Because a lot of credit
bureaus, they will stop--

00:56:50.670 --> 00:56:54.000
I mean, they will stop
taking into account

00:56:54.000 --> 00:56:56.910
of the default and
delinquency of some trade

00:56:56.910 --> 00:56:58.080
lines of the customers.

00:56:58.080 --> 00:57:01.410
And then, because of
the stimulation money,

00:57:01.410 --> 00:57:05.850
people will make extra
payments toward their debts.

00:57:05.850 --> 00:57:08.520
Again, all of the-- a
lot of factors here,

00:57:08.520 --> 00:57:12.060
but we found that the bureau
scores, they are inflated.

00:57:12.060 --> 00:57:14.830
So a lot of bureau
variables, they are inflated.

00:57:14.830 --> 00:57:19.570
And one today, when the
stimulation money went away,

00:57:19.570 --> 00:57:22.130
that's another factor animal.

00:57:22.130 --> 00:57:24.650
People's behavior,
they are shifting back.

00:57:24.650 --> 00:57:27.260
And again, because
of the COVID-19,

00:57:27.260 --> 00:57:29.120
the pandemic creates a bubble.

00:57:29.120 --> 00:57:30.740
And now the bubble burst.

00:57:30.740 --> 00:57:34.790
And when the people try to get
back to normal, all the risks,

00:57:34.790 --> 00:57:36.740
they were holding
in that bubble,

00:57:36.740 --> 00:57:38.370
now they are available now.

00:57:38.370 --> 00:57:41.180
So people in the
past three years

00:57:41.180 --> 00:57:43.550
during the pandemic,
a lot of loans,

00:57:43.550 --> 00:57:45.980
they were supposed
to go default,

00:57:45.980 --> 00:57:49.280
but they didn't because
of the maybe the stimulus

00:57:49.280 --> 00:57:51.050
money or a lot of other pauses.

00:57:51.050 --> 00:57:55.520
But right now, all that is over
suddenly, all of these loans,

00:57:55.520 --> 00:57:59.300
they began to-- they
begin to become delinquent

00:57:59.300 --> 00:58:03.300
or they begin to default. So I
mean, I saw a big, big shift.

00:58:03.300 --> 00:58:05.220
It creates a lot of
challenges for our team.

00:58:05.220 --> 00:58:09.210
So we are trying to manage
this processes right now.

00:58:09.210 --> 00:58:09.960
EMILIO: Thank you.

